From 36d8179c3a66f1c3fe1a74e48521e4bc5db0ef89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jan Schoeppach <jan.schoeppach@metax-gmbh.de>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:20:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] arm: socfpga: add Exor uSOM02 board (BeMoS)

U-Boot proper for the Exor uSOM02 module (Cyclone V SoC) on the BeMoS
carrier board. The Exor preloader stays in place, so the SPL is not
built. The environment location, size and variables are compatible
with the old Exor based U-Boot, so existing devices and the fw_setenv
based tooling keep working:
- env in eMMC user area at 0x200, size 0x1000
- mmc 0 = eMMC, mmc 1 = SD card (ulti_sdc in the FPGA)

Board specifics:
- release the HPS<->FPGA bridges after arch_early_init_r(), the SD
  card controller sits in the FPGA
- PHY setup as done by the Exor U-Boot (reg 0x17 = 0xb302)

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board specific, Exor uSOM02 / BeMoS]
